            "href": "https://www.scb.se/LE0105-en",
            "label": "Statistics page",
            "type": "text/html"
          }
        ]
      },
      "note": [
        "A statistical method is used to protect the data of individuals in the statistics presented. For this reason, the presented totals do not always equal the sum of their reported components. The method used for disclosure control is called Cell Key Method (CKM). You can read more about the method here: [Protection methods for disclosure control](https://www.scb.se/en/documentation/statististical-methods/protection-methods-for-disclosure-control/).",
        "Time in Sweden refers to the total time a person has been registered as a resident in Sweden and is given for people who have immigrated to Sweden.",
        "Ground for settlement are grounds for a residence permit. The table reports the last registered basis for residence for the person. Note that a person may have a decision basis that is several years old. EU citizens do not need to register their basis for residence at the Swedish Migration Board.",
        "The parents highest level of education refers to the parent with the highest level of education. Level of education refers to the highest education achieved at the end of the spring semester for the respective year.",
        "Students who have not received grades according to the goal  and knowledge based grading system are not included in the statistics.",
        "The statistics refer to individuals registered in the population register as of December 31 each year.",
        "Source:  \r\nSCB, STATIV (The Register for Integration Studies) and  \r\nSwedish National Agency for Education, the Register of Pupils in Compulsory School",
        "People with a foreign background are defined as persons who were born abroad, or born in Sweden with two parents born abroad. Persons with Swedish background are defined as persons who are born in Sweden with two parents born in Sweden or born in Sweden with one parent born in Sweden and one foreign born parent.",
        "To be eligible for the national programmes in upper secondary school, a student must have passing grades in Swedish/Swedish as a second language, English, and Mathematics. In addition, a passing grade in another five subjects is required to be eligible for the vocational programmes."
      ],
